  "id": "Compound::DB01056 - Gene::6331",
  "verbalization": "Tocainide is likely to interact with Scn5a through a shared pathway involving voltage-gated sodium channels. The evidence suggests that Tocainide binds to Scn7a and Scn8a, both of which participate in voltage-gated sodium channel activity, which in turn is participated by Scn5a. This implies that Tocainide may influence Scn5a via a common mechanism, possibly by modulating the activity of voltage-gated sodium channels. The consistent involvement of Scn5a in this pathway, despite the different target proteins, highlights a potential role for Tocainide in regulating sodium channel function, which could have implications for cardiac or neuronal activity. The overlapping pathways suggest that Tocainide may exert its effects on Scn5a through a mechanism that involves the modulation of sodium channel activity, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
